preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Hochschild Cohomology of Small Quantum Groups at Roots of Unity"
  authors:
    - family-names: Khairkhah
      given-names: Parham
      email: pkhairkh@icloud.com
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7048-1397"
  abstract: >-
    We propose the conjecture dim_C HH^2(u_q(g), C) = binom(n+1, 2) + 2|Phi^+|
    for any finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra g of rank n at an
    odd root of unity q = e^(2*pi*i/ell). The formula combines a Cartan-type
    contribution binom(n+1, 2) arising from the bialgebra cohomology of the
    bosonisation B^+ = B(V) # C[G] (mapped into HH^2 via the connecting
    homomorphism of the Mastnak-Witherspoon long exact sequence) with two
    copies of |Phi^+| ell-th-power classes [E_alpha^ell] and [F_alpha^ell]
    originating from the truncation relations in the Nichols algebra and its
    dual. We verify the formula by direct bar-complex computation for
    u_q(sl_2) at ell = 3 and ell = 5, where the computation gives
    dim HH^2 = 3 in agreement with the prediction. Explicit cocycle
    extraction at A_1 shows that none of the three HH^2 classes is supported
    on K-K pairs as a naive structural proposal predicted; the third (mixed
    E-F) class is identified as the image of the connecting homomorphism
    delta: H~^1_b(B^+) -> HH^2(D(B^+)) in the Mastnak-Witherspoon long exact
    sequence, and the LES decomposition dim HH^2(D(B^+)) = dim im pi-bar +
    dim im delta = 2 + 1 = 3 is verified numerically at A_1. We discuss the
    deformation-theoretic interpretation of these classes and the connection
    to the BCGP non-semisimple TQFT and to the -3/2 logarithmic correction
    of BTZ black-hole entropy.
  keywords:
    - Hochschild cohomology
    - quantum groups
    - roots of unity
    - Drinfeld double
    - Nichols algebra
    - BCGP TQFT
    - BTZ black hole
